  <description akvo:type="4" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BBB Colombia</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="6" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project stands out the collaboration between the Latin American partners of the DTZ Alliance through ICCO and Fly Free Movement has been consolidated since 2014.
The actions developed within the framework of the project will be harmonized with the guidelines and strategies of the policy line for the prevention and eradication of CSEC, the national strategy against trafficking in persons, the national business and human rights policy. And additionally, the actions will respond to local development plans in order to comply with the SDG 2030 agenda and the National Alliance against Violence against Girls, Boys and Adolescents, which includes two fundamental axes: on the one hand, the formulation of the public policy in a participatory manner and, at the same time, the mobilization of the entire society in the cultural transformation that leads us to generate a consensus of zero-tolerance with violence. This project is articulated with the actions proposed by the Flex Founds in a complementary way, it will reach new and a more significant number of the population of both social and institutional actors in the territory of La Guajira and will additionally allow the integration of actions in the city of Bogot&#xe1; not contemplated within the framework of Voice for Change, but which will allow the application of the methodologies that have been advanced in this last project to be developed with children, adolescents and young people from the capital, testing consolidated learning in other contexts</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will allow the consolidation and recognition of good practices for the comprehensive protection of child and adolescent victims of sexual exploitation and trafficking from an intersectoral approach. The bases are established for the generation and integration of alliances between the governmental, social-community and private sectors and especially linking girls, boys and adolescents, being an active voice and becoming leading actors in the defense and promotion of their rights.</narrative>
  </description>
